{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From twenty years old and upward.</b> Because one is not strong enough for warfare until twenty, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: 'twenty for pursuing.'" "<b>All who go forth to the army.</b> All who are fit to go forth in the army." "<b>In Israel,</b> to exclude the mixed multitude." "<b>You shall count them.</b> It did not say 'you shall number them,' for Israel was not counted by their heads; rather, it used the expression of counting (פקידה), which is an expression of providence — meaning that they should exercise providence over them, to know how many they are, and this providence was by means of the half-shekels." "<b>For their armies.</b> For they were many armies, and each and every tribe had a great army." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> תפקדו אותם לצבאותם — 'count them by their hosts' — this is what the verse says (Isaiah 43:4): 'מאשר יקרת בעיני נכבדת ואני אהבתיך.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Jacob: You are precious in My eyes, for I have fixed your image upon the throne of My glory, and with your name the angels praise Me, saying (Psalms 106:48): 'ברוך ה׳ אלהי ישראל מן העולם ועד העולם.' You are precious in My eyes, for to every nation I did not give a counting, but to you I gave a counting. A parable: to a king who had many threshing floors, all of them full of straw and chaff, and he was not particular about counting them. But one threshing floor he had, full of wheat — he said to his steward: Count for me how many kor are in it, how many modios are in it. The king — this is the Holy One, blessed be He. The threshing floor — these are Israel, as it says (Isaiah 21:10): 'מדושתי ובן גרני.' The grain — this is His holy nation, as it says (Jeremiah 2:3): 'קדש ישראל לה׳ ראשית תבואתה.' His steward — this is Moses, as it says (Numbers 12:7): 'בכל ביתי נאמן הוא.' So too the idolatrous nations are compared to straw and chaff, as it says (Job 21:18): 'יהיו כתבן לפני רוח וכמוץ גנבתו סופה,' and it is written (Obadiah 1:18): 'ובית עשו לקש.' But Israel are pure wheat; they are the righteous, as it says (Isaiah 60:21): 'ועמך כלם צדיקים לעולם יירשו ארץ.' Therefore He is particular about counting all of them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:40.820669648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}